# Review and merge

`main` is protected by the ruleset in `.github/rulesets/main.json`:

- Changes reach `main` only through a squash-merged PR; no force-push, no deletion, no bypass.
- These checks must pass: {% if stack_decided %}`checks` (the project's `just ci`), {% endif %}{% if release_workflow %}`image`, {% endif %}`gitleaks`; the ruleset in
  `.github/rulesets/main.json` is the list. Never merge on red, even when the failure looks unrelated: fix it or park the PR.
- Reviews are not required, for anyone: the author merges. CODEOWNERS also requests the owners of the paths it
  covers as reviewers.
- The author judges whether a PR is a **one-way door**: reverting it after release may not restore an equivalent
  state, because data is reshaped or dropped, a contract others depend on changes, data crossed a trust or tenancy
  boundary, an effect cannot be called back, or a governance file changes. The PR template asks, and the author
  labels it `door:one-way` and requests a review. Work on a one-way change stops, and the PR does not merge, until
  its ADR is accepted by the named decider (`CONSTITUTION.md` §5).

Review requests go through GitHub (CODEOWNERS requests them automatically), not chat. A PR still waiting for a
review after {{ review_wait_hours }} h is followed up by its author.

## Apply or change the ruleset

Edit `.github/rulesets/main.json`, merge it, then as a repo admin run `scripts/repo/apply-ruleset.sh`. The script
updates the ruleset named `main` or creates it.

## Symptoms

| Symptom | Fix |
|---|---|
| No reviewer requested automatically | The owner in `CODEOWNERS` is not a user or team with write access; fix the entry |
| Required check "Expected — waiting for status" never starts | A job in `ci.yml` was renamed; update `required_status_checks` and re-apply |
| `apply-ruleset.sh` returns 403 | Run it as a repo admin. Private repos on GitHub Free do not support rulesets |
